# .env.example
#
# PURPOSE
#   A committed template listing every environment variable the app needs, with NO real secrets.
#   Copy it to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in real values there.
#
# VARIABLES TO DEFINE (one per line as NAME=value in your .env)
#   POSTGRES_USER, POSTGRES_PASSWORD, POSTGRES_DB   - used by docker-compose to create the database
#   DATABASE_URL        - SQLAlchemy URL for the app DB (psycopg driver), pointing at localhost:5432
#   TEST_DATABASE_URL   - same server, separate database used only by pytest
#   LLM_PROVIDER        - which provider you use (e.g. google or openai)
#   LLM_API_KEY         - your API key (only ever in .env)
#   CHAT_MODEL          - a fast, cheap model with tool calling
#   EMBEDDING_MODEL     - an embedding model from the same provider
#   EMBEDDING_DIM       - its vector dimension; must match the vector(N) column in models.py
#   FRONTEND_ORIGIN     - Vite dev server origin, for CORS (default port 5173)
